<section class="section" id="deliverables"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading-grid"><h2>From a business problem to a clear next step.</h2><p class="section-lede">You leave with priorities you can act on, and a view of what to leave alone.</p></div><div class="deliverable-sequence"><article>{{ icon("search", "section-icon") }}<h3>Understand the business</h3><p>A structured intake followed by analysis of sales, costs, daily work, decisions and useful data.</p></article><article>{{ icon("compass", "section-icon") }}<h3>Choose where to act</h3><p>Your opportunities ranked, with the top three recommendations. Guidance on what to build, buy or automate.</p></article><article>{{ icon("notes", "section-icon") }}<h3>Leave with a plan</h3><p>A 90-minute executive session to go through the findings, with a concise roadmap for the next 90 days.</p></article></div><p class="comparison-note">When the evidence supports a number, I’ll estimate the impact. When it doesn’t, I’ll say so.</p></div></section>
<section class="section section-soft"><div class="shell recognition-grid"><div><h2>A better demo doesn’t settle the business case.</h2><figure class="audit-photo"><img src="/assets/images/adrian/at-work.webp" alt="Adrian Ching working at a laptop" width="909" height="1600" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div><div class="recognition-copy"><p>For example, if good leads aren’t getting followed up, generating more may only create a bigger pile.</p><p>First we need to understand what happens after the lead comes in, what gets missed and what that costs. It’s an example of where I would look, not a conclusion about your business.</p><p>That’s how the Audit works. I review the evidence before recommending the tools. Sometimes the useful fix is much smaller than the project you had in mind.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="fit"><div class="shell two-col"><article class="ruled-block"><h2>Who it’s for</h2><p>Established B2B companies with customers, sales and enough day-to-day activity for a better decision to matter.</p><ul class="editorial-list"><li>A real problem you want to address</li><li>An existing customer base, especially repeat buyers</li><li>Access to the relevant people and business data</li></ul></article><article class="ruled-block" id="scope"><h2>Where the work stops</h2><p>I diagnose and rank the opportunities. Implementation stays with your team or the people you choose.</p><p>This isn’t a build project, project management or a general introduction to AI. Very early companies without customers or business data are unlikely to be a fit.</p><a class="text-link" href="/advisory/">Need ongoing decision support? Explore advisory{{ icon("arrow", "link-arrow") }}</a></article></div></section>
